  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Robust, integrated and sustainable information systems - DHIS2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Robust, integrated and sustainable information systems (DHIS2) for improving health and well-being (2024-2028) aims to support countries and regions to strengthen their information systems and information architecture to achieve the SDGs in the health sector and beyond. DHIS2 is an open source free of charge health information system iin use in nearly 80 low- and middle-income countries. This program wil continue to maintain and develop DHIS2 as a Digital Public Goods by supporting core operations, strengthening in-country capacity and the HISP network, improve use and practices in the health sector and beyond, and make sure learning and innovation is shared globally. These priorities are integrated in the UiO/HISP strategy for 2023-2025 and will be integrated in the next strategy period 2026-2028. With climate change and more frequent extreme weather events having serious effects on health, DHIS2 is investing in a Climate and Health pilot in 10 LMICs which integrates climate and weather data into the health information systems. This will strengthen early warning and health response in climate related emergencies, and support countries in modelling the longer-term health effects to inform climate adaptation in the health sector.</narrative>
  </description>
